tmux is the terminal multiplexer. The active config keeps the default
prefix Ctrl+B and adds Ctrl+A as a secondary prefix for nested sessions.
Most bindings below require the prefix unless marked `direct`.

Current configuration:
	Prefix - Ctrl+b; secondary prefix - Ctrl+a
	Prefix e - Edit the local tmux configuration
	Prefix r - Reload the tmux configuration
	Direct Ctrl+l - Clear the pane and its history
	Prefix Ctrl+c - Create a new session
	Prefix Ctrl+f - Find and switch to a session
	Prefix Shift+Tab - Switch to the last session
	Prefix - / _ - Split below / split right
	Prefix h/j/k/l - Focus pane left/down/up/right (repeatable)
	Prefix > / < - Swap pane down/up
	Prefix + - Toggle/maximize the current pane
	Prefix H/J/K/L - Resize pane left/down/up/right by 2 (repeatable)
	Prefix Ctrl+h/Ctrl+l - Previous/next window (repeatable)
	Prefix Ctrl+Shift+h/l - Move current window left/right
	Prefix Tab - Switch to the last window
	Prefix m - Toggle mouse support
	Prefix F - Run the configured path picker

Copy mode (vi keys):
	Prefix Enter - Enter copy mode
	v - Begin selection; Ctrl+v - Toggle rectangular selection
	y - Copy selection to the tmux buffer and exit; Escape - Cancel
	H/L - Start/end of line
	Prefix y - Export the top tmux buffer to the system clipboard when available

Paste buffers:
	Prefix b - List paste buffers
	Prefix p - Paste the top buffer
	Prefix P - Choose a buffer

High-frequency tmux defaults (reference; n/p are overridden here):
	Prefix c - New window; Prefix , - Rename window
	Prefix d - Detach; Prefix & - Kill window
	Prefix n/p - Next/previous window (the current config uses Ctrl+l/Ctrl+h)
	Prefix 0-9 - Select window 0-9
	Prefix z - Zoom/unzoom the current pane
	Prefix [ / ] - Enter copy mode / paste the top buffer
	Prefix ? - List key bindings; Prefix : - Command prompt

The local Oh My Tmux layer is sourced after the main file. `mouse` starts
disabled in the local file; Prefix+m toggles it and reports the new state.
